# End-to-end EMULATOR test: Anycubic Kobra Go (HDSC HC32F460) under
# Renode in tick mode. Boots real firmware, completes identify +
# clocksync, brings up the full config (4 plain step/dir steppers, 2
# software-PWM heaters, fans, endstops, 2 thermistors) and reads both
# thermistors. See "Per-printer tests" in test/emulator/README.md for
# the shared conventions.
#
# The Kobra Go has no Trinamic drivers, so there is no TMC round-trip
# here; the new ground (hc32f460_smoke covers boot only) is the HC32 ADC:
# hc32f460_adc_stub.py serves M4_ADC1 @ 0x40040000. klipper's
# src/hc32f460/adc.c kicks a conversion by writing STR=1, polls
# ISR.EOCAF, then reads the 16-bit DRn result (DR0 @ 0x50, channel index
# = (off-0x50)/2). The HC32 ADC layout matches no upstream Renode model
# and hc32f460.repl maps no ADC, so the stub is the only thing at that
# base. A broken ADC sits at temp=0.0 with no shutdown, so the temp=3
# assertion below is the positive proof samples arrived. Hotend reads
# channel 13 (PC3, ATC Semitec 104GT-2), bed channel 11 (PC1, EPCOS).
DICTIONARY hc32f460-serial-PA3PA2.dict
CONFIG anycubic_kobra_go.cfg
EMULATOR anycubic_kobra_go.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
G4 P2000
M105

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
